 p1630:{t:'P-1630 \u2014 NGL Pipeline Pump #1 (M2175)',d:['\u2248360 GPM @ ~8,873 ft TDH \u00B7 700 HP \u00B7 plunger pump','Takes booster discharge (532/533-10\u2033) \u2192 NGL pipeline','Suction pulsation dampener \u00B7 start-up strainer \u00B7 PSV-1630A set 2400 psig','Confirmed real, direct OEM nameplate photo: change oil every 2000 hrs, 4-quart capacity, required oil options Mobil 1 SHC 626 (ISO 68), Phillips Syncon R&O Oil 68, or Royal Purple Synfilm GT68']},
 p1635:{t:'P-1635 \u2014 NGL Pipeline Pump #2 (M2175)',d:['\u2248360 GPM @ ~8,873 ft TDH \u00B7 700 HP \u00B7 plunger pump','Discharge recycles via FCV-1422 to V-1422 or runs through A-1322 product cooler','Suction pulsation dampener \u00B7 PSV-1635A set 2400 psig','Confirmed real, direct OEM nameplate photo: change oil every 2000 hrs, 4-quart capacity, required oil options Mobil 1 SHC 626 (ISO 68), Phillips Syncon R&O Oil 68, or Royal Purple Synfilm GT68 (same nameplate spec as P-1630, consistent with matched pump pair)']},
 f518:{t:'518-10\u2033 demeth bottoms \u2192 V-1422',d:['TIED IN: T-1521 bottoms (via LV-1521) \u2192 surge tank','UNVERIFIED OVERLAP, FLAGGED NOT CORRECTED: the P\u0026ID M2150 detail pass (see xv1521/line518 entries under Demethanizer \u0026 Reboilers) separately documents an instrumented XV-1521 ESD valve on this same line, with its own ZSO/ZSC-1521 position feedback. LV-1521 here already has its own real, distinct XSY-1521 trip solenoid (see the lv/lt entries) \u2014 these read as two genuinely different valves (a modulating level-control valve plus a separate emergency shutdown valve in series), which is a completely normal P\u0026ID pattern, but this has NOT been field-verified against the real P\u0026ID side by side. Flagging rather than guessing \u2014 confirm with Ryan whether LV-1521 and XV-1521 are both real and distinct, or whether one source used an inconsistent tag for the same physical valve.']},
 f1260:{t:'1260-8\u2033 stabilized NGL product outlet',d:['Pipeline-pump discharge through A-1322 product cooler and outlet pressure control','Continues through verified outlet metering to V-8000 pig launcher and NGL pipeline; see indexed NGL product P&IDs','NOTE: the toolbar dropdown option for this same line still labels it \u201c(open)\u201d \u2014 left as-is since fixing that is a separate small edit, flagged here so it does not get missed']},
