 return mSVG(s)+'<div class="note">Verified NGL path retained and clarified without removing controls: V-1422 surge tank -> one of P-1619/P-1620 booster pumps -> common booster discharge -> one of P-1630/P-1635 pipeline pumps -> common pipeline-pump discharge -> PT-1630B -> FIT-1630A (combined common-header flow) -> A-1322 product cooler -> FT-1422 -> 6-inch FCV-1422 recycle branch back to V-1422 OR forward through the parallel PCV-1623 / PCV-1624 pressure-control paths to Plant Outlet. PIT-1630A and PIT-1635A remain on the individual pipeline-pump suction branches. P-1619/1620 and P-1630/1635 retain RUN/STOP and RED TAG controls; a red-tagged stopped pump cannot be started. A-1322 fan motors now also have individual red-tag controls. PCV-1623 is governed by the LIC-1422B / PIC-1623 pair, and PCV-1624 by LIC-1422C / PIC-1624. Verified DCS flow-permit logic is applied independently to PY-1623 and PY-1624 from FT-1422: FT-1422 >291.50 GPM is required to initially permit each outlet valve to open; FT-1422 <265.00 GPM interlocks that valve closed. The 265.00-291.50 GPM deadband retains the previous permit state and prevents chatter. FT-1422 is calibrated to the operator-observed normal envelope: AUTO remains at or below about 377 GPM, while the 385-GPM FIC-1422A setpoint remains the high-flow recycle threshold; high tank level is handled by opening the two forward outlet paths and biasing recycle closed rather than inventing 400+ GPM circulation. With the permit healthy, putting PIC-1623 or PIC-1624 in MAN exposes CV −/+ and the operator can position that outlet PCV directly; loss of the flow permit remains a hard interlock that overrides MAN and closes the valve. FCV-1422 has the same MANUAL CV control for recycle. Verified 12AU staging rule: one booster pump must be running before a pipeline pump can run. With the train running, discharge is always routed either to recycle, split between recycle and sales, or fully to sales with recycle closed; a pipeline pump is never allowed to run with no booster supply. All existing trend points and live process values remain. 12CU material balance: V-1422 inflow is the sum of demethanizer NGL plus any stabilizer product actually routed through P-5060/P-5065 to XV-5040B; recycle through FCV-1422 returns to V-1422 and therefore is not counted as net outlet.</div>'
