var CF3D_PID_M2000_12HI={"number":"020185-AE-DW-M2000","revision":"2","page":1,"title":"Inlet Area / Pipeline Pig Receiver","sourceFile":"2026-10-04 10-42.pdf","sha256":"e4cccfb7be62632af6de3270231271033ea8c2b69cd20358510833452f24b0ff","byteLength":744610,"imageOffset":2437,"imageLength":741853,"mime":"application/pdf","base64":"","status":"ISSUED FOR CONSTRUCTION; supplied scan Rev 2, not proof of current as-built revision","scope":"Entire sheet visually reviewed in two passes. Minor 1/2-inch tubing/root fittings are recorded at source level, not individually routed in 3D. No major equipment moved; no operating logic changed.","reviewed":"2026-10-04","facts":[{"id":"equipment","tags":["V-1000"],"text":"V-1000 is the inlet gas pig receiver. Drawing marks 24 x 30 in, 1440 PSIG at 130 F, material CS, no insulation and no heat tracing, with a 30-in quick-opening closure. These are drawing design markings, not operating setpoints. Existing vessel dimensions and position are not changed.","location":"Upper equipment data / receiver outline","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"receiver","tags":["V-1000","XV-1000A","XV-1000B","XV-1000C"],"text":"Incoming pipeline divides between a receiver bypass through XV-1000A and a receiver inlet through XV-1000B. The downstream-of-XV-1000B receiver-side takeoff returns through XV-1000C to the common plant inlet header. XV-1000A/B/C are each marked 24 in and FL; FL is retained as printed, not converted to a commanded valve state.","location":"Left half, pipeline / receiver branches","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"main","tags":["V-1000","ESD-1000D","PV-1010A"],"text":"Common line 1002-24\"-GP-D1-5L passes ESD-1000D (24 in, FC) then the 24 x 16 transition, PV-1010A (16 in, FC), and 16 x 24 transition. Manual block item 200013 follows PV-1010A. A D1-5L / B1-X52 specification break is shown.","location":"Lower centre / yellow-highlighted control valve","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"outlet","tags":["PV-1010A","V-1020","C-5700","PIT-1010A","PIT-1010B"],"text":"PIT-1010A and PIT-1010B taps are drawn downstream of PV-1010A. Line 1003-24\"-GP-B1-X52 continues through 24-in manual block 200042 to V-1020 on M2020. Line 1194-3\"-GP-B1-CS-1.5\"HB connects with C-5700 on M2560 before that outlet block; direction/source role follows the retained operator return identification, not an arrow inferred here.","location":"Lower-right main inlet / match lines","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"esdbypass","tags":["ESD-1000D"],"text":"ESD-1000D has a distinct 2-in bypass around the ESD only (not around PV-1010A): manual items 200008 and 200010, with CSC marked on 200010.","location":"Below ESD-1000D","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"psv","tags":["PSV-1000","V-1000"],"text":"PSV-1000: 3/4 x 1 in, D orifice, SET at 1440 PSIG, THERMAL. Separate relief branch on line 1002 upstream of ESD-1000D. Line 1427-1\"-RF-D1-5L has 1-in CSO block 200045 and a 1 x 0.75 transition at the PSV inlet. The PSV outlet expands 1 x 2 and passes 2-in CSO block 200047 into line 1428-2\"-RF-A0-CS to M2901. Small 0.5-in bleed item 200046 is recorded but not drawn as separate tubing.","location":"Centre PSV callout / relief takeoff","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"vent","tags":["V-1000","RO-1000"],"text":"A separate 2-in receiver relief/vent route 1001-2\"-RF-A0-CS continues to M2901. It includes manual item 200030 (2 in) and RO-1000 marked 0.25 in. The 0.25 marking is the restriction-orifice callout, not the main inlet pipeline diameter.","location":"Lower-left receiver branch / relief continuation","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"regulators","tags":["PCV-1000E","PCV-1010A","PV-1010A"],"text":"PCV-1000E is marked 0.5 in on the receiver-actuator pneumatic network with AIR CYLINDER. PCV-1010A is a separate 0.25-in pneumatic regulator on the M2922 instrument-air supply to PY-1010A / PV-1010A. PCV-1010A is NOT an alias of the 16-in process valve PV-1010A. No regulator set pressure is legible/supplied.","location":"Upper-left actuator air cylinder / above PV-1010A","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"pressure","tags":["PIT-1000","PIT-1000A","PI-1000B","PI-1000C","PI-1000D"],"text":"PIT-1000 is on the incoming pipeline ahead of the receiver isolation arrangement. PIT-1000A is on line 1002 upstream of ESD-1000D. Local PI-1000B is on the receiver-side inlet, PI-1000C on the bypass/header, and PI-1000D on the receiver branch. Instrument manufacturer, calibrated ranges and numeric alarm setpoints are not established by this sheet.","location":"Left / central pressure taps","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"position","tags":["ZI-1000","ZSC-1000D","ZSO-1000D","ZT-1010A"],"text":"ZI-1000 is marked PIG SIG, Note 2. ZSC-1000D and ZSO-1000D are ESD closed/open feedback; ZAC/ZAO indications and XS-1000D OPEN PERM are signal functions, not extra process valves. ZT-1010A provides PV-1010A position indication via ZI/ZY-1010A.","location":"Receiver inlet / above ESD and PV","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"controls","tags":["ESD-1000D","PV-1010A","PIC-1010A"],"text":"Sheet includes PIC-1010A/PY-1010A, HS-1010A LC OVERRIDE from LIC-5010A on M2505, and signal continuations FROM LDAHH-1020/M2020, LDAHH-1025/M2025 and LDAHH-1030/M2030. Documented signal relationships are reference-only here; existing trips, permissives, loops and operating setpoints are not overwritten.","location":"Upper-right control/continuation lines","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"manual","tags":["V-1000","ESD-1000D","PV-1010A","PSV-1000"],"text":"Manual item numbers retained from this sheet: 200028 (2-in NC, XV-1000A bypass); 200001 (2-in NC, XV-1000C bypass); 200022 and 200032 (6-in capped receiver connections); 200034 (2-in connection between receiver inlet sections); 200008 and 200010 (2-in ESD bypass; 200010 CSC); 200013 and 200042 (24-in main blocks); 200030 (2-in receiver vent); 200045 (1-in CSO PSV inlet) and 200047 (2-in CSO PSV outlet). Item numbers are drawing identifiers, not newly invented MV field tags.","location":"Receiver / ESD / PV / PSV manual symbols","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"small","tags":["V-1000","ESD-1000D","PV-1010A"],"text":"Small-bore source inventory retained without full 3D tubing: 200004/200005, 200019/200024, 200020/200027, 200025/200026, 200029, 200006/200007, 200011/200018, 200014/200015, 200016/200017, 200021, 200023, 200033, 200046. Exact item specifications remain visible on the original sheet; unverified line schedules/ratings are not inferred from these codes.","location":"Instrument roots / pneumatic feeds / bleeds","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"future","tags":["V-1000","V-1020"],"text":"FUTURE INLET PIG RECEIVER and FUTURE SLUG CATCHER connections are explicitly marked. Items 200043/200044 and 200041/200040 belong to those future connections, not proof of installed extra vessels or a current active flow path.","location":"Below/above lower inlet header","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"continuations","tags":["V-1000","V-1020","C-5700","PSV-1000"],"text":"Off-page references: M2020 process continuation to V-1020; M2020/M2025/M2030 LDAHH signal continuations; M2505 LIC-5010A signal; M2560 C-5700 line 1194; M2901 relief lines 1001 and 1428; M2922 instrument air. Follow the continuation sheets before declaring complete field piping or isolation boundaries.","location":"Right/lower drawing borders","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED; FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"}],"pending":["Exact field coordinates, adjoining installed ratings/schedules and manufacturer/model details not established by the drawing.","The existing HMI uses PIT-1010B on the upstream pressure domain; M2000 Rev 2 draws PIT-1010B downstream of PV-1010A. Model tap follows the drawing, but no live value or controller reassignment is made; reconcile with field/DCS.","Future connection construction status is not known; no future vessel is created.","Minor 1/2-in tubing and individual instrument-root valves are retained in the drawing/source inventory but intentionally not modeled one-by-one.","No flow-meter primary element is identified on this sheet; RO-1000 is not promoted into a flow transmitter.","Receiver 30 x 24 detail and field nozzle dimensions require mechanical/field reconciliation with the fixed schematic receiver shell; its geometry is preserved."]};
