var CF3D_PID_M2020_12HJ={"number":"020185-AE-DW-M2020","revision":"2","page":2,"pages":[1,2],"title":"Inlet Area / Slug Catcher #1","sourceFile":"2026-10-04 11-11.pdf","sha256":"c8b019297faa842d78e27038d4c57ca28fc34846f339a04a40d9e994469d734c","byteLength":1212838,"images":[{"page":1,"offset":2444,"length":563375,"mime":"image/jpeg","rotation":-90},{"page":2,"offset":566350,"length":646066,"mime":"image/jpeg","rotation":0}],"mime":"application/pdf","base64":"","status":"SOURCE_DRAWING_REVIEWED; TWO VIEWS OF ONE REVISION; NOT FIELD_VERIFIED","scope":"Refine existing connections. Major equipment and process destinations retained; only missing source-supported relief/components added. No controllers, limits or operating settings changed. Minor tubing remains source-only.","facts":[{"id":"identity","location":"Title and revision block","tags":["V-1020","M2020"],"text":"020185-AE-DW-M2020 Rev 2, Inlet Area / Slug Catcher #1. Both uploaded pages are scans of this same drawing and revision, not separate equipment or independent drawings. Both pages were reviewed as one source; original PDF bytes are omitted in learn-only mode.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"equipment","location":"V-1020 design annotation","tags":["V-1020"],"text":"V-1020: SLUG CATCHER #1; 108-in OD x 60-ft-0-in S/S; 715 PSIG at -20/120 F. These are drawing design annotations, not a current pressure setpoint. Existing simplified equipment geometry and placement have not been resized to these annotations.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"inlet","location":"Left inlet / central expansion","tags":["V-1020","V-1000","V-1025","1003","1004"],"text":"1003-24-in-GP-B1-X52 arrives from V-1000 / M2000. The sheet shows a 24 x 36 transition and 1004-36-in-GP-B1-X52 continuing to V-1025 / M2025. Retain existing routing; do not create another receiver or slug catcher from the second scanned page.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"gas","location":"Upper right continuation","tags":["V-1020","V-1030","1005"],"text":"Gas continuation 1005-20-in-GP-B1-X52 is labelled V-1030 / M2030. Exact continuation reconciliation requires that sheet; the existing common gas-header connection remains in place.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"liquid","location":"Lower right continuations","tags":["V-1020","V-1025","1342","1006"],"text":"Two distinct hydrocarbon-liquid lines continue to V-1025 / M2025: 1342-20-in-HC-B1-X52-1.5-in-HU-ETW and 1006-4-in-HC-B1-X52-1.5-in-HU-ETW. The 1006 outlet shows a 6 x 4 transition. Do not combine the 20-in and 4-in lines or invent an off-page destination.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"relief","location":"Upper-left PSV callout","tags":["V-1020","PSV-1020A","1263"],"text":"PSV-1020A: FIRE case, SET AT 715 PSIG; 3-in Class 300 inlet x 4-in Class 150 outlet; L orifice. Four-inch inlet piping reduces 4 x 3 to the valve; the 4-in outlet expands to 6-in relief piping. Outlet 1263-6-in-RF-A0-CS continues to M2901. This is a relief reference only, not a simulator trip/setpoint or field test certificate.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"relief_blocks","location":"Upper-left relief isolation group","tags":["PSV-1020A","202005","202004","V-1020"],"text":"PSV inlet manual block 202005 is 4-in, B2RF-H2, marked CSO. Outlet block 202004 is 6-in, marked CSO; full specification-code readback remains pending. The 0.5-in bleed 202006, Z2TF-H2, is indexed from the sheet but not individually rendered. CSO markings are documentation, not authorization to isolate relief protection.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"bypass","location":"Below PSV relief group","tags":["PSV-1020A","202003","202007","V-1020"],"text":"The separate two-inch bypass around the PSV group contains manual valve 202003, B8RF-H2, marked CSC, followed by check valve 202007, B4R-H2, toward the relief outlet. The drawing shows a B1-X52/A0 specification break. This is not an automatic ESD, and the model does not operate the bypass.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"level","location":"Lower horizontal vessel","tags":["V-1020","LIT-1020","LG-1020B","LG-1020C","LG-1020D","LSHH-1020B","LSLL-1020B","LY-5010A"],"text":"The lower vessel shows GWR LIT-1020, level gauges LG-1020B/C/D, LSHH-1020B with LAHH-1020B, and LSLL-1020B with LALL-1020B. LIT-1020 has a signal continuation to LY-5010A on M2505; this is a control signal, not a process pipe. No numeric thresholds or new controller actions are assigned from these symbols.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"upper_level","location":"Upper separation-chamber instruments","tags":["V-1020","LG-1020A","LSHH-1020A","LSH-1020A","DPI-1020"],"text":"The separation chamber shows LG-1020A, LSHH-1020A / LAHH-1020A, LSH-1020A / LAH-1020A, and DPI-1020 with tappings across the separator section. Individual impulse tubing is intentionally not modeled. The mounted 3D instrument symbols do not establish surveyed nozzle/bridle positions.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"manual_index","location":"Package instrument and drain valves","tags":["V-1020","V-001","V-002","V-003","V-004","V-005","V-006","V-007","V-008","V-009","V-010","V-026","V-027","V-028","V-029","V-030","V-035","V-036","202008","202009","202001"],"text":"Source-only package item index, not a field lineup: V-001/V-002/V-003/V-004 are 2-in NO level-bridle blocks; V-005 through V-010 are 0.75-in NO gauge blocks; V-026 is 2-in NO, V-027/V-028 are 4-in NO, V-029/V-030 are 0.75-in NO; V-035 is 4-in NO and V-036 is a check on the chamber-to-storage connection. GWR bridle blocks 202008/202009 are 3-in. Item 202001 is 2-in on the inlet. These package-local V-numbers are scoped to V-1020 / M2020, not globally unique plant tags. Exact mount/bridle and remaining hardware placement are pending.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"minor","location":"Small tubing / drawing scope","tags":["V-1020","DPI-1020","LIT-1020"],"text":"Small 0.5-in and 0.25-in tubing, vents, bleeds and minute fittings remain available on the original P&ID and in retained source notes, but are not all rendered. No new regulator or flow meter is identified on this sheet; RO/DP/level symbols must not be converted into invented flow meters.","status":"DRAWING_REVIEWED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"preserve","location":"Operator refinement policy","tags":["V-1020","M2020"],"text":"Keep existing connections and process destinations. Refine size/alignment/inline fittings in place; add only a verified missing connection or component after identity matching. Keep vessels, compressors, pumps and other major equipment fixed. The unrelated incoming pipeline now approaches grade at 45 degrees by extending its existing external end only.","status":"OPERATOR_INSTRUCTION / IMPLEMENTATION_SCOPE"}],"pending":["Final 24/36-in inlet and 20-in gas nozzle sizing must be reconciled to the fixed, simplified vessel envelope before enlarging tightly spaced takeoffs. Do not force colliding pipes or move the equipment.","M2025/M2030 are needed to reconcile the separate 1342/1006 liquid and 1004/1005 gas continuations. Existing main process destinations are preserved; the separate 20-in liquid connection is not guessed.","Package level-bridle manual-valve placement, DPI tapping positions, instrument manufacturer/model/range and PSV manufacturer/serial/test certificate remain pending. Small 1/2-in tubing is intentionally not detailed."]};
