INFO.release12jz={"t":"12JZ - C-4100 / C-4200 inlet-compressor vendor update","d":["Source-scoped C-4100/C-4200 inlet-compressor vendor presentation, from 12JY. The two banks are parallel first-stage odd/even throws, not two serial stages. Keep equipment at its existing site location; distinguish source data, uncertain readbacks and schematic geometry. Major equipment and principal piping are visible; fine accessories are selectable, with all indexed details in the owning compressor notebook, Reference Library and Finder. No live process, control, trip, historian or saved-data behavior is changed. Original PDF/photo bytes are not embedded.","Parallel first-stage odd/even banks; manual VVCP, not residue FVCP.","Ten inlet-package PSV source records: four process and six local AIR; unknown nameplate details remain pending.","PSV-4102 source readback conflict and BV-4231 revision conflict retained.","Source-scoped C-4100/C-4200 inlet-compressor vendor presentation, from 12JY. The two banks are parallel first-stage odd/even throws, not two serial stages. Keep equipment at its existing site location; distinguish source data, uncertain readbacks and schematic geometry. Major equipment and principal piping are visible; fine accessories are selectable, with all indexed details in the owning compressor notebook, Reference Library and Finder. No live process, control, trip, historian or saved-data behavior is changed. Original PDF/photo bytes are not embedded.","The source pages are two five-sheet inlet-compressor sets. Unit-specific source ownership, degraded readbacks and source conflicts remain visible.","Normal 3D view omits minor tubing/labels. A searchable reference record does not imply a verified physical device location.","No new actual plant setpoints or valve commands are created. Readbacks are not field inspection, relief sizing or a LOTO procedure.","The field-data list is a review of available simulator/source records, not a certified site-wide PSV register.","Original source media remain learn-only metadata; no PDF or photograph is embedded or sent on ordinary Ryan questions."]};


INFO.release12jy={"t":"12JY - Residue compressor vendor model and per-unit notebooks","d":["Vendor-source presentation update for C-6100/C-6200/C-6300 only. Retain individual source pages and the printed X-to-unit mapping. Major equipment and process piping are visible; fine tubing, instrument racks and signal details are retained under the owning compressor and selectively revealed. Source ratings, regulator settings and valve markings are reference facts, not current values, implemented trip limits or an approved lineup. All site routing, elevation, head/support and accessory geometry is schematic unless an explicit dimension is recorded. No process, historian or saved-data behavior is changed.","Source: 2026-10-12 09-45.pdf, 15 pages, three five-sheet sets.","C-6100/C-6200/C-6300 retain their site locations and existing external cooler paths. Six distinct throws, two scrubbers and four pulse vessels per unit are now modeled.","Three process-gas PSV records per unit are reused, not duplicated. Four local instrument-air reliefs per unit have distinct atmospheric outlets and are never connected to the hydrocarbon flare.","Main motor, one-fan frame-oil cooler, oil filter, three-way temperature valve, frame-oil pump assembly, sub-base catch bottle and separate air-powered catch pump are distinguished.","Reference Library: Residue compression / C-6100 (or C-6200/C-6300) / Vendor drawings. The click-for-info panel has the same five-section notebook and unit-specific component index.","Fine detail starts OFF. Select one compressor, then Fine detail - selected unit; the other two stay clean. All reference-only devices remain available through Finder Full component / nameplate record without a guessed exact location.","15 source drawings; 1284 source records (not a certified count of discrete installed field assets).","107 gallons EXCLUDING PIPING is the frame oil reference capacity, not the oil catch-bottle volume or a fill instruction.","Vendor source says alarm/shutdown details await completed I/O list and operating sequence. No process-control code or saved-data keys were changed.","Vendor-source presentation update for C-6100/C-6200/C-6300 only. Retain individual source pages and the printed X-to-unit mapping. Major equipment and process piping are visible; fine tubing, instrument racks and signal details are retained under the owning compressor and selectively revealed. Source ratings, regulator settings and valve markings are reference facts, not current values, implemented trip limits or an approved lineup. All site routing, elevation, head/support and accessory geometry is schematic unless an explicit dimension is recorded. No process, historian or saved-data behavior is changed.","The 15 pages are three five-sheet unit sets, not 15 compressors. Template X mapping is explicit; operating readings, serial numbers and actual load-step state are not cloned across units.","Per-compressor sections and detailed records are stored as extracted references. Original PDF/photo bytes are not embedded in the deployment.","No individual vendor hose, impulse tube or rack signal is falsely represented as a new full-size field valve; detailed records remain searchable when deliberately omitted from the clean overview.","Fine non-visual records are source references. Parent focus is navigation only, not a fabricated exact device location.","Previously modeled process relief header destinations remain source-qualified; this update does not certify relief hydraulics, materials, slopes, current valve positions or whole-plant collision clearance."]};








